{
  "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8036-946a-ce7ff06748a9",
  "title": "Lombok",
  "sourceUrl": "https://xpandeyed.notion.site/20924eb1ed548036946ace7ff06748a9",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8053-84d8-d23d31782cfa",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Generate repetitive Java methods"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8053-84d8-d23d31782cfa-b0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Lombok is an optional Java library that generates methods and constructors from annotations."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8053-84d8-d23d31782cfa-b1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The compiler processes these annotations while building the class. They do not generate methods when the application runs."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8053-84d8-d23d31782cfa-b2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot does not require Lombok. You can write the same methods yourself."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8053-84d8-d23d31782cfa-b3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Configure Lombok for your build and IDE. Annotation processing must be enabled where your setup requires it."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80af-bb03-d47212966157",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Choose the annotation"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lombok-annotations",
      "type": "table",
      "columnOrder": [
        "0",
        "1"
      ],
      "hasColumnHeader": true,
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "lombok-annotations-r0",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "Annotation"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "Generated code"
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "lombok-annotations-r1",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "@Getter"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "A getter for each applicable field."
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "lombok-annotations-r2",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "@Setter"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "A setter for each non-final applicable field."
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "lombok-annotations-r3",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "@NoArgsConstructor"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "A constructor with no arguments."
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "lombok-annotations-r4",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "@AllArgsConstructor"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "A constructor for non-static fields. Initialized final fields are excluded."
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "lombok-annotations-r5",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "@RequiredArgsConstructor"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "A constructor for uninitialized final fields and uninitialized @NonNull fields."
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "lombok-annotations-r6",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "@ToString"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "A toString method."
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "lombok-annotations-r7",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "@EqualsAndHashCode"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "equals and hashCode methods."
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "lombok-annotations-r8",
          "type": "table_row",
          "cells": {
            "0": [
              [
                "@Data"
              ]
            ],
            "1": [
              [
                "Getters, setters for non-final fields, toString, equals, hashCode, and a required-arguments constructor."
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lombok-data-choice",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Use specific annotations when you need only some of these methods. @Data does not mean that every class gets a no-argument or all-arguments constructor."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80da-9b86-db2e0ef1d6ef",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Write a data class"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-805d-a8bb-c6315f8a15b6",
      "type": "example",
      "example": {
        "title": "Generate User methods with Lombok",
        "description": [
          "Add Lombok to the build and configure annotation processing.",
          "This class represents simple application data."
        ],
        "code": "import lombok.Data;\nimport lombok.NoArgsConstructor;\nimport lombok.AllArgsConstructor;\n\n@Data\n@NoArgsConstructor\n@AllArgsConstructor\npublic class User {\n    private String name;\n    private int age;\n}\n",
        "language": "java",
        "explanation": [
          "@Data generates accessors, toString, equals, and hashCode for this class.",
          "@NoArgsConstructor provides new User().",
          "@AllArgsConstructor provides new User(name, age).",
          "Generated toString, equals, and hashCode use the fields unless you configure exclusions."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f8-8e61-cf70f0b8485f",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Control the generated behavior"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f8-8e61-cf70f0b8485f-b0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Do not generate setters for fields that callers should not change."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f8-8e61-cf70f0b8485f-b1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Generated toString can include private or sensitive fields. Exclude fields that must not appear in logs."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f8-8e61-cf70f0b8485f-b2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Avoid applying @Data automatically to JPA entities. Relations and mutable fields can make generated equality or toString inappropriate."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f8-8e61-cf70f0b8485f-b3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Bidirectional relations can cause recursive toString calls. Select or exclude relation fields explicitly."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f8-8e61-cf70f0b8485f-b4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A JPA entity needs a public or protected no-argument constructor. Choose that visibility when generating it."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f8-8e61-cf70f0b8485f-b5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Lombok constructors do not create Spring beans. Dependency injection still follows Spring’s constructor and bean rules."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80f8-8e61-cf70f0b8485f-b6",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Jackson mapping and Bean Validation still follow their own rules. Generating accessors does not replace their configuration."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
